  "privacy": {
    "effective": "16 September 2026",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The short version",
        "body": [
          "Your affirmations stay on your phone. There is no account and no sign-in, and what you write is never sent to us or to anyone else. Li also sends anonymous usage statistics, which are part of how Li works and cannot be turned off."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "What Li stores, and where",
        "body": [
          "Your affirmations, which ones you have favorited, and your settings (theme, motion, notification time) are saved only in Li’s private storage on your device.",
          "We cannot see, read or recover any of it."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Anonymous usage statistics",
        "body": [
          "To learn which features are used and what to improve, Li sends anonymous usage events to PostHog, our analytics provider, hosted in the EU. For example: that an affirmation was favorited, that a theme was chosen, that the app was opened, or how many affirmations and favorites a library holds.",
          "These events never include the text of your affirmations, what you search for, or the names or contents of files you import. Li has no account and does not know who you are: events are linked only to a random ID created on your phone.",
          "Along with each event, PostHog receives basic technical details: device model, operating system and version, app version, language and time zone. PostHog uses your IP address to estimate your country and city, and does not store the IP address with the events.",
          "These statistics are part of how Li works and there is no setting to turn them off. If you would rather not send them, uninstalling Li stops them completely."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "What Li does not do",
        "body": [
          "Li does not ask for your name, email or any account details, does not show ads, and does not sell your data or share it with anyone for advertising."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Notifications",
        "body": [
          "If you turn on the daily affirmation, Li schedules the notifications on your device. No notification service or server is involved, and you can turn it off at any time in Settings or in your phone’s settings."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Importing and sharing",
        "body": [
          "When you import a text file, Li reads it on your device and keeps only the affirmations it finds.",
          "When you share an affirmation or a backup, you choose where it goes (for example a chat app or email). From then on it is handled by that app, under its own privacy policy."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Backups by your phone",
        "body": [
          "If Android backup is turned on, your phone may include Li’s data in your personal Google account backup, so it can come back when you set up a new phone. That backup is handled by Google, not by Li."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Deleting your data",
        "body": [
          "You can delete all affirmations from Settings → Danger zone. Uninstalling Li removes everything it stored on your device."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Children",
        "body": [
          "Li is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect information from anyone."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Changes to this policy",
        "body": [
          "If Li ever starts handling data differently, this policy will be updated before that change is released, and the date below will change."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Downloaded content",
        "body": [
          "Li downloads its themes, images and texts (such as this policy) from GitHub and jsDelivr, so they can be updated without a new version of the app. Like any website, those services receive your IP address when the app downloads from them. Nothing about you or your affirmations is sent."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Contact",
        "body": [
          "Questions about privacy: danielgu.contact@gmail.com"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
